  "reviewed_runtime_boundaries": [
    "World 1, 6 and 9 difficulties use direct public level 14, 49, 50, 66, 75 and 84 values, while encounter member 108 uses direct public level 44 values; no interpolation is used.",
    "The inactive cycle uses Chilling Lament followed by Frosty Absorption; Freezing Point then alternates Everwinter Rain with the enhanced Chilling Lament.",
    "Chilling Lament deals 250% Ice damage to the primary target; while in Freezing Point, a Frozen primary target receives an additional 100% Ice damage.",
    "Everwinter Rain deals 200% Ice damage to all opponents and applies one-turn Freeze at 60% base chance; Freeze deals delayed 100% Ice damage.",
    "Weakness Break removes Freezing Point, marks the public reset path, and makes the next sequence restart with Chilling Lament followed by Frosty Absorption.",
    "The Freezing Point marker, Freeze delayed damage, frozen-target bonus and Weakness-Broken reset use shared Rule IR without a native handler."
  ]
